<title>AUSTRIA: Austria finmin mulling oil, tobacco tax hike - paper.</title>
<headline>Austria finmin mulling oil, tobacco tax hike - paper.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-05-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian Finance Minister Rudolf Edlinger is considering raising taxes on oil and tobacco in a bid to help fill a 25 billion schilling ($2.1 billion) hole in the country's 1998 budget, a newspaper reported on Saturday.</p>
<p>Daily Der Standard said the medium-term budget for 1998 foresees a deficit of 2.6 percent of gross domestic product (GDP) after 2.7 percent this year.</p>
<p>Experts tip Austria as being among the first to qualify for Europe's single currency, whose criteria stipulate that a country's budget deficit should not surpass 3.0 percent of GDP. ($ = 11.91 Austrian Schillings)</p>
</text>
